  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1100 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nMonday will be hot, but hopefully not record-setting as the big \nridge weakens further and additional atmospheric moisture \nincreases the chance for scattered storms. Those rain and storm \nchances will creep up more for Tuesday into Wednesday as a trough\ndevelops to our north and pushes a frontal zone toward our area. \n\nThe troughing pattern will deepen mid to late week, pushing the\nfront down through our area. This will drop temperatures\nsignificantly, although they will still be on the warm side or\nnormal. The NBM remains optimistic about late week with highs in \nthe upper 70s to low 80s and overnight lows in the upper 50s to \nlow 60s. Not remarkably cool for this time of year, but oh so much\nbetter than this heatwave! The cooler air will also be drier, so \nlate week rain chances will be low. This is bad news for crunchy \nlawns as Tuesday's showers and storms may not amount to enough \nmoisture to turn around the worsening drought.",
